"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin the painted chrome of the form controls against Chrome 159 on
Linux: the checkbox check mark, the radio dot, the `<select>` arrow, the
`<textarea>` resize grip, the native (`appearance: auto`) frame and fill of an
unstyled text field / button, the UA colours of a disabled control, and --
at device scale 4 -- the device-px height of the painted control box.
Audience: web renderer paint / Draw IR / device-scale maintainers.

Chrome oracle: Chrome for Testing 159.0.8154.6 aarch64, `--headless=new
--disable-gpu --hide-scrollbars --force-device-scale-factor=K
--screenshot`, 300 CSS px wide, the two pages below (Liberation Sans, the
13.333px UA control font). Page A holds one default control per 44 px band (a
textarea band is 70 px); page B holds the catalog's
`padding:8px;border:1px solid #94a3b8;border-radius:5px` controls.

Every fact is measured relative to the control's own box (found by its
non-white bounding box in its band), so a layout offset of the box does not
count as a paint difference. Chrome / base 0251987783a / this change:

| fact                                   | Chrome            | base              | now      |
|----------------------------------------|-------------------|-------------------|----------|
| checkbox, px differing by > 8 (of 169) | 0                 | 52                | 0        |
| checked checkbox, same                 | 0                 | 169               | 25       |
| check mark ink box (red >= 160)        | c2-10 r2-9        | c2-10 r2-10       | = Chrome |
| radio / checked radio, px differing    | 0 / 0             | 76 / 143          | 0 / 26   |
| disabled checkbox ring, fill           | d1d1d1 f8f8f8     | 2563eb f8fafc     | = Chrome |
| select arrow, px differing (12 x 9)    | 0                 | 44                | 4        |
| select arrow ink box from right / top  | c-12--5 r7-11     | c-13--7 r7-10     | = Chrome |
| textarea grip, #666 px from the corner | c-9--3 r-9--3 n10 | none              | = Chrome |
| text field top edge, 2nd row, right    | 767676 ffffff ... | 767676 767676 ... | = Chrome |
| text field value ink rows              | 6-17              | 9-17              | = Chrome |
| button frame, 2nd row, face            | 767676 efefef x2  | 767676 x2 ffffff  | = Chrome |
| styled button face                     | efefef            | ffffff            | = Chrome |
| disabled field frame, fill             | d0d0d0 f8f8f8     | 767676 ffffff     | = Chrome |
| disabled button frame, face            | d0d0d0 eeeeee     | 767676 ffffff     | = Chrome |
| disabled select frame, fill, arrow     | dddddd fafafa a5a5a5 | 767676 ffffff ffffff | dedede fafafa a5a5a5 |
| K=4 heights select textarea input button | 139 198 133 133 | 140 192 132 132   | = Chrome |
| K=4 check mark ink box                 | c8-43 r8-41       | c8-43 r8-43       | = Chrome |
| K=4 checked radio, centre column       | B4 W6 a1 B30 a1 W6 B4 | B4 W8 B28 W8 B4 | = Chrome |
| K=4 select arrow ink                   | c-49--18 r29-45 n94 | c-55--28 r28-43 n256 | = Chrome |
| K=4 grip ink                           | c-40--12 r-40--12 n170 | none         | = Chrome |

Open (not pinned here): Chrome rounds the native frame (outer radius 2.5 px,
so the four corner px are page colour) -- the frame is square here; the
checked marks differ from Chrome by 25 / 26 edge px at scale 1 (Skia's small
stroke is slightly bolder than its exact area); the control font is carried as
13 px, so `Simple` ends one column early (42, Chrome 43).
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-WEB-FORM-CHROME-PAINT-001 — native form-control parts paint as Chrome 159 paints them, at device scale 1 and 4.
"""
# @tag: unit, browser_engine, paint, form_control, device_scale, chrome159
